    {
      "text": "turboderp titled the change “TP: Refactor/fix auto allocation.” The parent tensor-parallel planner used remaining memory as a split weight, passed zero total weight to its proportional splitter when all devices ran out of room, and emitted logical chunk indices even when a chunk represented multiple channels. Attention always offered individual KV heads as split units, regardless of head width.",
